{
  "key": "gh-918",
  "fields": {
    "summary": "Rework legs cannot fix CRAP/method_size/format violations — no dart toolchain in the leg env",
    "description": "**Evidence:** dart #408 (CRAP 9.00, fixed by operator), #413 rework legs 08:56/09:22Z reported success but left method_size violations in place, #414 needed an operator refactor (UpgradeCommand.run CC=12, 94-line test main) on 2026-10-16. Legs have no dart SDK: they cannot run `dart analyze/test/format` or `crap4dart check` to see or verify gate violations.\n\n**Ask:** factory setup for dart repos provisions a cached dart SDK (same channel the repo's quality.yml uses) and exposes it on PATH for the leg session, so rework legs can reproduce the gate output locally before claiming success. Same pattern as the golden-test Flutter toolchain for fa legs. Without this, the SM dead-zone fix (sibling issue) just produces rework legs that flounder.\n\n## Machine jobs\n- [x] ▶ dev (fa-bug-dev) · [run](https://github.com/IstiN/dmtools-agents/actions/runs/38893334998) · started 11:22 · done 11:43 ✅"
  }
}

